# {{META_REPO_NAME}}

<!-- HELIX:BEGIN overview -->
This is a Helix coordination meta repo.

It owns:

- repo registry in `repos.yml`
- workspace or feature-space artifacts in `workspaces/`
- Helix runtime state in `.helix/`
- Helix-managed docs, scripts, and templates in `helix/`
- Copilot runtime-facing files in `.github/`

It does not own product code. Product repos are attached from the registry only when a workspace needs them.

## Start Here

1. Update `repos.yml` with the repos Helix can use
2. Create or edit `workspaces/<workspace-id>/workspace.yml` using `helix/templates/workspace.yml.template` as the starter shape when needed
3. Run `./helix/scripts/setup-workspace.ps1 -Workspace <workspace-id>`
4. Optional: run `./helix/scripts/set-context-provider.ps1 -Provider code-review-graph -Mode review-only`
5. Start Helix from the active meta repo workspace

## Helix Docs

- `helix/docs/helix-process.md` — canonical lifecycle and loops
- `helix/docs/helix-instance-schemas.md` — manifest shapes and validation rules
- `helix/docs/helix-core-meta-repo-model.md` — packaging model for installed versus source layout

## Key Paths

- `.github/` — agents, prompts, skills, and Copilot instructions
- `helix/` — installed Helix-managed docs, scripts, and templates
- `.helix/` — install state, active workspace pointer, repo-state, generated state
- `.helix/context-providers.yml` — optional graph retrieval switches and budgets
- `workspaces/` — feature-space artifacts, including task boards and decisions
- `repos.yml` — repo registry

Legacy root `decisions/` and `task-boards/` directories are deprecated. Keep those artifacts under `workspaces/<workspace-id>/...`.
